# No one-symbol collector workaround

Collector code is the shared machine. Per-symbol facts live on the position or template. The code reads those settings. It does not embed them.

A workaround is a fail when it exists so one symbol works: a hardcoded URL, percent, amount, interval, or `if symbol == …` branch. The fix is to read the stored setting, or add a setting if the machine cannot express the case, then use that path for every name that has the setting.

A new interval is allowed when it is data. It is not allowed as a special case in code for one ticker.
